03:50:21,070 --> 03:50:24,996
How do we interpret the width of these bars and their placement on the x-axis?

2341
03:50:25,486 --> 03:50:26,916
It's not immediately clear.

2342
03:50:27,854 --> 03:50:34,276
To make our histogram more clear, and to help us get the answer to our run frequency question, we need to do some more work.

2343
03:50:35,136 --> 03:50:44,324
Right now, the hist function is free to pick its own bar width, and with rest gaps this small, it slices our data into bars thinner than a single day.

2344
03:50:45,166 --> 03:50:50,180
Back in the hist function call, we take control of the bar width with the bins argument.

2345
03:50:51,214 --> 03:50:55,780
This argument is a list of numbers marking where one bar ends and the next begins.

2346
03:50:56,846 --> 03:51:04,004
We build that list with the range function, starting at min rest days, or in other words, our shortest rest.

2347
03:51:04,846 --> 03:51:16,036
We end it at max rest days, plus two, plus one to reach past our longest rest, and plus one more because the range function stops one short of the number we give it.

2348
03:51:16,942 --> 03:51:18,148
Running the cell again,

2349
03:51:19,118 --> 03:51:20,612
